  "content": "<b>Meaning/Usage</b>: Used frequently by restaurant servers to tell customers the food is almost ready\n<b>Explanation</b>: This can be used in a sentence, but is commonly used by itself.\n\"Your order is <b>coming right up</b>.\"\n\"It's <b>coming right up</b>!\"\n\"Your food is <b>coming right up</b>.\"\n<b>A.</b> \"Did you order the cheeseburger with french fries?\"\n<b>B.</b> \"I sure did.\"\n<b>A.</b> \"It's <b>coming right up</b>.\"\nOther Common Sentences\n\"Your food will be right out.\"\n\"Your order is coming out quickly.\"",
